-- title:
--   Sections of a resolved model avoid the edge points
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $N_0$ nonzero and $p$ prime, assume $p \nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak P$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package $\mathfrak P : \mathtt{DRModelPackageLevel}\ N_0\ p$ for that non-divisibility. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain together with a ring homomorphism $\rho_O$ from the base ring $\mathtt{DRLevel.R}\ p$ to $O$, and assume the maximal ideal of $O$ is generated by the image of $p$; let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ with a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$. Let $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}$ be a resolved package $\mathtt{DRResolvedModelPackageLevel}\ N_0\ p\ \mathfrak P\ O\ \rho_O\ \kappa\ \mathrm{to}\kappa$, so in particular it carries a scheme $Y$, a proper flat structure morphism $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{toBase} : Y \to \operatorname{Spec} O$ regular away from the basic open of $p$, a finite type $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{node}$ with widths $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{width}(n) \ge 1$, and a family of invertible ideal sheaf data $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{comp}(c)$ indexed by $c \in \mathtt{X0MqComponents}\ \mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{width} = \mathrm{Fin}\ 2 \oplus \coprod_{n} \mathrm{Fin}(\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{width}(n) - 1)$ whose product of ideals is the ideal generated by $p$. Finally let $\sigma$ be a section, that is a morphism of schemes $\operatorname{Spec} O \to Y$ whose composite with $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{toBase}$ is the identity of $\operatorname{Spec} O$. Write $y = \sigma(\mathfrak m_O)$ for the image under $\sigma$ of the closed point of $O$. The conclusion is threefold: $y \ne \mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{edgePt}(n,d)$ for every node $n$ and every $d \in \mathrm{Fin}(\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{width}(n))$; $y$ lies in the open set $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{smoothOffEdges}$; and there is exactly one index $c$ with $y$ in the support of the ideal sheaf data $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{comp}(c)$.
--
--   This is the standard fact that an integral point of a regular model lands in the smooth locus of the model, here in the form needed for the resolved Deligne–Rapoport models of $X_0(N_0p)$: a section over $O$ meets the fibre over $p$ in a point which is neither one of the distinguished points $\mathrm{edgePt}(n,d)$ attached to the nodes nor on two components at once, so that a single component of the special fibre is attached to the section. It is used in the construction identifying the pullback along $\mathrm{toDR}$ of the product of the component ideal sheaves, via [`ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackageLevel.exists_pullback_toDR_iso_foldr_ker_tensor_invModule_prod_comp`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackageLevel.exists_pullback_toDR_iso_foldr_ker_tensor_invModule_prod_comp).
